Written 2026-10-01 10:22 AEST by a Spark brief-writer sub-agent for Wednesday, from `723dc0722b68`, `m365-integration.openapi.ts` read at every line named here and the handler(s) read. Source: KS-1364 (Backlog, assigned to Kamil; created by Peter 2026-09-28 with the sweep-4 evidence): "One for the spec when convenient". Carve: this brief takes `POST /api/onedrive/files/{id}/sync` from the ticket's 17-operation table.

## The mode - read this twice

CODE+TEST. Your diff touches EXACTLY 2 files, in this order:
1. `Blockchain/Dev/services/m365-integration/src/m365-integration.openapi.ts` - modified in place, `--- a/Blockchain/Dev/services/m365-integration/src/m365-integration.openapi.ts` / `+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/m365-integration/src/m365-integration.openapi.ts`, EXACTLY the 1 hunk(s) given below, byte for byte.
2. `Blockchain/Dev/services/m365-integration/src/__tests__/ks1364-onedrive-file-sync-body-required.test.ts` - a NEW file: `--- /dev/null` then `+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/m365-integration/src/__tests__/ks1364-onedrive-file-sync-body-required.test.ts`, ONE hunk `@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@`, every line `+`.

You never touch any other file. The `reference_test_file` in your input (the security service's KS-747 spec test) is shape reference only - do NOT touch it.

## What is wrong (one paragraph)

The registration for `POST /api/onedrive/files/{id}/sync` (`m365-integration.openapi.ts:816`-`:850`) declares its request body as a multi-line `body: {` block (`:824`-`:834`) whose only key is `content:` (an inline zod object requiring a non-empty `connectionId`, `:830`), with no `required`, so the published spec says the body is OPTIONAL. The handler says otherwise: `index.ts:1050` (`app.post('/api/onedrive/files/:id/sync', ...)`) destructures `connectionId` from `req.body` (`:1052`) and answers 400 "connectionId is required" when it is falsy (`:1053`); the service runs express 4 (`package.json:20`), so an absent body arrives as an empty object and is always a 400. KS-1364's sweep 4 measured exactly that: 5 cases, all 400. The ticket's direction is verbatim: "mark `requestBody.required: true` where the handler's Zod schema rejects an absent body, at the generator (`*.openapi.ts`)". In the multi-line form the house shape is a `required: true,` line inside the `body:` block (`kyc.openapi.ts:474`).

## Where

- `:833` - the closing `},` of the body's `content:` object; it stays, and a `required: true,` line is inserted AFTER it, before the body's own closing `},` at `:834` (insertion site)

## The exact change

ONE hunk, a PURE INSERTION of one line (old side 6, new side 7). Nothing is removed. The new line is `      required: true,` at SIX spaces, the same indent as `content: {` (`:825`) and its closing `},` (`:833`). Its three lines of leading context are the end of the inline schema (`.passthrough(),`, then `},` at eight spaces, then `},` at six); its trailing context is `    },`, `  },`, `  responses: {`. Every context line is non-blank.

