/**
 * =============================================================================
 * M365-INTEGRATION SERVICE — OpenAPI registrations
 * =============================================================================
 *
 * Microsoft 365 surface: Entra ID OAuth, SharePoint sites + documents,
 * OneDrive files, Teams webhooks, Outlook add-in OBO flow. Production-
 * active per project memory (M365 Business Basic license, SharePoint
 * integration live).
 *
 * Graceful degradation: the service starts and serves /health even when
 * M365 env vars are missing. SharePoint / auth operations return HTTP 503
 * until a valid M365 license + Entra app registration are configured.
 *
 * Endpoints registered (22 routes, 18 unique paths). The api-gateway
 * proxies the connections / sites / documents / outlook / callback subset
 * through /api/m365/* (rewriting ^/api/m365 → /api), and proxies the
 * onedrive / teams subset directly without rewrite. Public-facing paths
 * therefore split as:
 *   Connections (Entra ID OAuth):
 *     - GET    /api/m365/callback             — OAuth redirect target
 *     - POST   /api/m365/connections/init
 *     - POST   /api/m365/connections/complete
 *     - GET    /api/m365/connections/{id}
 *     - DELETE /api/m365/connections/{id}
 *     - POST   /api/m365/connections/{id}/refresh
 *   SharePoint sites:
 *     - POST   /api/m365/sites
 *     - GET    /api/m365/sites
 *     - GET    /api/m365/sites/{id}/libraries
 *     - DELETE /api/m365/sites/{id}
 *   SharePoint documents:
 *     - POST /api/m365/documents/sync
 *     - GET  /api/m365/documents
 *     - GET  /api/m365/documents/{id}
 *   OneDrive (gateway passthrough — no /api/m365 prefix):
